Top-Down Approach in Data Warehouse
Important exam topic
1. Definition
The Top-Down Approach is a method of designing a Data Warehouse in which we first create a large, centralized Data Warehouse for the entire organization. After that, smaller Data Marts are created for individual departments.

In simple words:

First create one big Data Warehouse, then divide the required data into smaller department-wise Data Marts.
